#!/bin/sh
# Rejects a commit that stages a file over 20,000 bytes, so every file stays small enough for an
# agent to read whole. Binary files and paths .gitattributes marks linguist-generated or
# linguist-vendored are skipped: agents do not write them.

max_bytes=20000
tab=$(printf '\t')
too_big=

# -z keeps quotes, backslashes, and tabs in paths unescaped. Binary files show "-" for their
# line counts.
while IFS=$tab read -r added _ path; do
	[ "$added" = - ] && continue
	git check-attr --cached linguist-generated linguist-vendored -- "$path" |
		grep -Eq ': (set|true)$' && continue
	bytes=$(git cat-file -s ":$path")
	[ "$bytes" -gt "$max_bytes" ] &&
		too_big="$too_big  $path: $bytes bytes
"
done <<LIST
$(git diff --cached --numstat --no-renames --diff-filter=ACM -z | tr '\0' '\n')
LIST

[ -z "$too_big" ] && exit 0

cat >&2 <<MESSAGE
pre-commit: these staged files are over $max_bytes bytes:
$too_big
Split each one, then stage the result and commit again:

1. Find the seams: groups of items that change together and share private helpers,
   such as one view, one state machine, one operation, one test journey, or the tests.
2. Rust: turn foo.rs into foo.rs plus foo/<part>.rs files, declared in foo.rs with
   "mod <part>;". Re-export what callers use with "pub use" or "pub(crate) use" so no
   caller changes. Move a large "#[cfg(test)] mod tests" into foo/tests.rs.
   crates/ui/src/native_view/menu.rs and menu/ show the pattern. Never add foo/mod.rs.
3. Integration tests: split tests/foo.rs by journey into tests/<journey>.rs files that
   share helpers through tests/support/, loaded with #[path = "support/<file>.rs"].
4. Markdown: move each large section into its own file beside the original and link to it.
5. Move code as is. Do not rewrite, rename, minify, or drop comments or tests while splitting.
6. Leave each new file well under the limit, near 12,000 bytes, so the next change fits.
7. Run cargo fmt --all, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked
   -- -D warnings, and cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked.
8. Stage the new files and the shortened original: git add <files>.

A file no agent writes, such as a lockfile or generated code, belongs in .gitattributes
as linguist-generated instead.
MESSAGE
exit 1
